      "pronunciationText": "Each subshell is made of orbitals, the regions where an electron is likely to be found. An s subshell has one orbital, a p subshell has three, a d has five, and an f has seven. Here's the key rule. Each orbital holds at most two electrons, and those two must spin in opposite directions. We draw each orbital as a box, and its electrons as an up arrow and a down arrow. So an s subshell holds two electrons, p holds six, d holds ten, and f holds fourteen.",
