      "pronunciationText": "So which subshells fill first? Electrons fill the lowest energy subshells first, just as a ball settles on the lowest step of a staircase. Mostly, that means level by level. One s, two s, two p, three s, three p. But there's a surprise at level four. The four s subshell is lower in energy than three d, so four s fills first, and three d fills after it.",
